# Netscape HTTP Cookie File
# https://curl.se/docs/http-cookies.html
#
# SoundWave downloads with the YouTube session stored in cookies.txt. YouTube blocks most
# anonymous downloads ("Sign in to confirm you're not a bot"), so downloads and channel
# syncs need real cookies here. Export them from a private browser window signed in to
# YouTube with a local exporter ("Get cookies.txt LOCALLY" for Chrome, not the lookalike
# "Get cookies.txt"); README.md "YouTube Cookies" has the steps. Put the exported lines
# in `cookies.txt` (NOT this example file).
#
# The container reads this file and writes YouTube's refreshed session back after each
# download, so it must be writable: owned by 1000:1000, chmod 600, no ":ro" mount.
#
# ⚠️ Treat cookies.txt as a SECRET — it grants access to the Google account it came from
#    (use a secondary account). It is gitignored on purpose; never commit real cookies.
